209
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:15,599
If we take the limit as delta x becomes

210
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:18,160
very small, the sum becomes an integral.

211
00:08:15,599 --> 00:08:23,120
The integral along the ray of mu of x dx

212
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:25,120
equals the natural log of ni / n o.

213
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:27,599
So in the discrete domain, we speak of a

214
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:29,520
ray sum, a summation. And in the

215
00:08:27,599 --> 00:08:31,919
continuous domain, we speak of a line

216
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:34,320
integral, an integral along the x-ray

217
00:08:31,919 --> 00:08:36,399
path. Either way, x-ray measurements

218
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:38,880
provide ray sums or line integrals of

219
00:08:36,399 --> 00:08:40,800
the attenuation field. With this model

220
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:42,800
in mind, we can now discuss why the

221
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:47,159
resulting linear system can have a

222
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:47,159
unique solution, at least heristically.

223
00:08:48,959 --> 00:08:52,320
This is what I call the onion peeling

224
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:54,240
idea.

225
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:56,720
Think of a picture and decompose it into

226
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:58,160
a collection of pixels.

227
00:08:56,720 --> 00:09:00,080
The pixel does not have to be

228
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:03,040
rectangular. Here I use triangular

229
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:05,519
pixels. I perform the decomposition into

230
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:08,000
